  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT10-042#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT10-042 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, all of your opponent's Digimon with either <Security Attack +X> or <Security Attack -X> are affected by \"can't attack this Digimon and can't activate [When Attacking] and [When Digivolving] effects.\"",
        "question": "Does \"can't attack this Digimon and can't activate [When Attacking] and [When Digivolving] effects\" in this card's [Opponent's Turn] effect apply to opponent's Digimon with <Security Attack +X> as well as those with <Security Attack -X>?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it has ＜Security A. +1＞ as soon as the digivolution is complete, so this card's effect prevents the [When Digivolving] effect from activating.",
        "question": "My opponent has this Digimon in play, and I digivolve one of my Digimon into a Digimon card that has ＜Security A. +1＞ and a [When Digivolving] effect. Does that Digimon activate its [When Digivolving] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "It refers to Digimon affected by <Security Attack +> or <Security Attack -> effects.",
        "question": "What kind of Digimon does this effect's \"Digimon with <Security Attack>\" refer to?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, <Security Attack> is not canceled even if a Digimon has both ＜Security A. +1＞ and <Security Attack -1>. The Digimon is considered to have <Security Attack>, so the effect applies to this Digimon.",
        "question": "If an opponent's Digimon has both ＜Security A. +1＞ and <Security Attack -1> so the values cancel each other out, is the Digimon treated as not having <Security Attack>, and is it unaffected by \"Digimon with <Security Attack> can't attack this Digimon and can't activate [When Attacking] and [When Digivolving] effects\"?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it activates. [BT9-015 MetalGreymon (X Antibody)] gains ＜Security A. +1＞ from the [When Digivolving] effect, so after that effect has activated, this card then prevents further [When Attacking] and [When Digivolving] effects from activating.",
        "question": "I digivolved one of my [MetalGreymon] into [BT9-015 MetalGreymon (X Antibody)]. It gets <Security Attack+1> and +3000 DP with its [When Digivolving] effect, but does that effect activate when my opponent has this Digimon in play?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it doesn't.",
        "question": "If a Digimon has a <Security Attack> effect that is only active when certain conditions are met, such as \"While this Digimon has X or more digivolution cards, it gains ＜Security A. +1＞,\" does this card's [Opponent's Turn] effect apply when these conditions aren't met?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "The attack continues. This effect doesn't end or cancel an attack if the attacking Digimon gains <Security Attack> after the attack has been declared. It prevents Digimon with <Security Attack> from declaring the attack.",
        "question": "My opponent has this Digimon in play. One of my Digimon that doesn't have <Security Attack> attacks it, and then the attacking Digimon gains <Security Attack> from a [When Attacking] effect or an effect such as \"when one of your Digimon attacks\".  What happens to the attack?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, \"When... attacks\" effects are not [When Attacking] effects, so this card's effect can't stop them from activating.",
        "question": "When a Digimon with <Security Attack> attacks, does this card's effect stop \"when this Digimon attacks\" effects of those Digimon, such as ＜Raid＞?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
